topics.detail:
AI Harms Society argues that AI is fundamentally unethical. AI Limitations argues that AI is unhelpful in publishing and fiction. AI is unnecessary for tasks that can be done already.

@mgerrydoyle.bsky.social: “yeah, I would say of all the things in the world that ai is neither welcome nor helpful in, it's publishing and especially fiction I want a person responding to my words and helping me improve them, not an algorithm that has gobbled up decades of bestseller lists in "learning…”

AI Harms Society (51.5%) says AI is fundamentally unethical. AI Limitations (48.5%) says AI is not helpful in certain areas.

AI Falls Short argues that AI is not beneficial. AI Disclosure argues that Companies should disclose AI use.

@thatqueerharpy.bsky.social: “its either too good and its AI or its so bad its AI. You can't win. I'm sorry this happened to you. Keep being goated, King.”

AI Falls Short (90.6%) says AI is not beneficial. AI Disclosure (9.4%) says Companies should disclose AI use.

AI Harms Us argues that AI is not beneficial. AI Impact argues that AI has limited economic benefits. AI Exploitation argues that AI work is done by exploited humans.

@josephpolitano.bsky.social: “So much of the value of AI infrastructure is embedded in imports rather than US production that the boom in AI investment has had much less impact on GDP than headline figures suggest, even flipping negative this quarter as import growth outstrips investment growth”

AI Harms Us (43.3%) says AI is not beneficial. AI Impact (30%) says AI has limited economic benefits. AI Exploitation (26.7%) says AI work is done by exploited humans.

AI Is Excessive argues that AI consumes insane energy resources. AI collects everyone's data without a purpose. AI will eventually be beaten out by people trading privacy and creativity for personal gain. AI Limitations argues that AI can be misled by poisoned training data. AI cannot learn grammar or represent semantics accurately. AI is not a replacement for careful analysis and peer-reviewed research. AI requires significant relearning for each agent without shared knowledge.

@xenolandscapes.com: “She thinks it's structurally impossible for AI to be doing the things that people claim it is useful for, because you can't learn grammar from just data and can't perform it through statistical prediction, and can't represent semantics via distributions of terms.”

AI Is Excessive (66.7%) says AI is out of control. AI Limitations (33.3%) says AI has significant limitations.

World.detail:
Palestinian Rights argues that People who support Russian expansion do not genuinely support Palestinian self-defense. Israel's government and military are committing genocide against Palestinians. Israeli Privilege argues that Israelis are protected by the media.

@jcmartinofba.bsky.social: “The Israeli soldier who RAPED Palestinians on camera is being paraded around shows in Israel and treated like a celebrity star. In 2002, Rabbi Eyal Karim said soldiers are allowed to rape non-Jewish women in wartime.”

Palestinian Rights (71.8%) says Palestinians deserve rights. Israeli Privilege (28.2%) says Israelis are protected by the media.

Hebron Demolitions argues that Demolitions in Hebron follow an attack on Israeli soldiers. Forced displacement of Palestinians from their homes in Hebron is a form of punishment. Israeli Occupation argues that Israel expands occupation in south Syria. US supports Israeli occupation. Israel occupies Lebanese territory. Israel occupies Syrian territory. Arab nations call for end to occupation. Israel's occupation sparks protests.

@jcmartinofba.bsky.social: “After the Israeli settlers stole as many olives as possible from the Palestinian olive harvest....and after a Washington Post reporter was assaulted and diplomats from many countries were attacked the next day.... NETANYAHU is illegally locking down all of the West Bank.”

Hebron Demolitions (72.4%) says Israel demolishes homes in Hebron. Israeli Occupation (27.6%) says Israel occupies parts of Syria.

Environment.detail:
Stop Deforestation argues that Deforestation harms the environment. Tree Appreciation argues that Trees are valued.

@jimferguson.bsky.social: “Leaf Color Report: The #woods are still very green. The maples have turned red and yellow, but the oaks are waiting for some frosty temperatures. #photography #trees #forest #leaves”

Stop Deforestation (55.6%) says Deforestation harms the environment. Tree Appreciation (44.4%) says Trees are valued.

Other.detail:
Mother Enables Abuse argues that Mother prioritizes husband over child's safety. Mother calls child a liar about abuse. Mother fails to protect child from rapist husband. Mother Rights argues that a mother should not have her baby taken away. A mother would do anything to defend her child. A mother should not be punished for protecting her child. A mother's actions to protect her child should not be called murder.

@psgamer92.bsky.social: “Yeah, the ad is not about calling out Amy for being a liar. I mean it’s ridiculous to use the mother who sided with her daughter’s rapist when she was 12 and frame it as if Amy is the dishonorable one here. No, the ad is about attacking victims of predators.”

Mother Enables Abuse (77%) says Mother enables husband's abuse of child. Mother Rights (23%) says Mothers should protect their babies.
